## SECTION 1: PROJECT OVERVIEW

### What is LineageLens?

LineageLens is an AI provenance tracking system for software teams. It answers one question that no existing tool answers: **"Where did this code come from, and why?"**

As AI coding assistants — Claude Code, Cursor, Aider, GitHub Copilot — write increasing fractions of production codebases, the origin and intent of code becomes invisible. LineageLens makes it visible again. It captures every significant AI-assisted code insertion, links it to the prompt and model that produced it, stores it with structured metadata, and gives developers tools to search, explain, audit, and govern that code over time.

The detection host is currently a VS Code extension. The backend is a self-hosted FastAPI service backed by PostgreSQL and optionally Neo4j. Both work together: the extension observes file changes in real time, the backend stores and indexes provenance records across a team.

### The Problem

AI coding tools are now writing large portions of production software. This creates three compounding problems:

**Auditability.** When a bug appears in AI-generated code, there is no record of what prompt produced it, which model generated it, or what context surrounded the decision to insert it.

**Governance.** Security and compliance teams cannot answer basic questions: How much of our codebase was AI-generated? Which files have the highest AI insertion density? Which sessions produced high-risk code (security patterns, auth logic, eval calls)?

**Lineage.** Code evolves. When AI-generated code is refactored, extended, or deleted, the relationship between generations is lost. There is no graph of how AI-contributed code has changed over time.

Traditional tools — debuggers, linters, code review bots — operate on what the code does, not where it came from. LineageLens is the missing layer that tracks origin, not behavior.

### Why This Matters

The risks are concrete. A prompt that was slightly wrong, a model that hallucinated an API, a session that wrote auth logic without full context — these are real failure modes that have caused real incidents. Without provenance, root-cause analysis guesses. With it, you can trace from the bug back to the exact AI session that wrote the code.

For regulated industries — fintech, healthcare, defense — AI code governance is becoming a compliance requirement. LineageLens gives teams the audit trail they need before regulators require it.

### Target Users

**Base users.** Individual engineers using AI tools heavily who want a personal record of what AI wrote in their codebase. They run LineageLens Base: local-first, no shared team features, just capture and explain.

**Plus workspaces (5-50 engineers).** Teams shipping AI-assisted code who need shared provenance records, semantic search across all insertions, governance dashboards, and the ability to review AI contribution patterns. They run LineageLens Plus.

**Max organizations.** Large teams with compliance requirements, multi-workspace setups, full graph lineage tracking, and audit export needs. They run LineageLens Max with Neo4j-backed lineage graphs.

