## SECTION 6: DEPLOYMENT & ENVIRONMENT

### Docker Compose Bundles

Three separate Docker Compose configurations, one per tier:

| File | Tier | Services |
|---|---|---|
| File | Tier | Services |
|---|---|---|
| `deploy/docker-compose.base.yml` | Base | postgres, backend |
| `deploy/docker-compose.plus.yml` | Plus | postgres, backend |
| `deploy/docker-compose.max.yml` | Max | postgres, neo4j, backend |

All backends build from `backend/Dockerfile`. Postgres uses `pgvector/pgvector:pg16` image. Neo4j uses the official `neo4j` image.

### Quickstart Scripts

```
scripts/quickstart-base.sh       # Base: 7-step setup
scripts/quickstart-plus.sh       # Plus: 7-step setup
scripts/quickstart-max.sh        # Max: 7-step setup
```
Each script:
1. Checks prerequisites (docker, openssl, curl, python3)
2. Stops any existing containers (preserving volumes)
3. Generates secrets with `openssl rand` if `.env` is absent; validates existing `.env` if present
4. Starts PostgreSQL and waits for health
5. Runs `alembic upgrade head`
6. Starts the backend and waits for `/health` 200
7. Prints the health response and getting-started commands

