## SECTION 9: PRODUCT POSITIONING

### What Makes LineageLens Unique

No other tool tracks the provenance of AI-generated code. There are tools that:
- Review code for bugs (linters, CodeQL, SonarQube)
- Review code for security (Snyk, Semgrep)
- Track who changed code (git blame)
- Generate code explanations (LLM chat)

None of them answer: **"This function was written by an AI — which one, in response to what prompt, and what risk signals did the generated code contain at the time of insertion?"**

LineageLens is the first system that captures provenance at insertion time, stores it persistently, and surfaces it at review time.

### Differentiation from Traditional Debugging Tools

| Traditional Debugging | LineageLens |
|---|---|
| Looks at what code does | Looks at where code came from |
| Operates at runtime or static analysis | Operates at write time |
| Knows the author is a human | Knows which AI tool wrote it |
| Requires a bug to exist | Captures context before a bug appears |
| Has no concept of "prompt" | Stores the prompt that produced the code |
| No model provenance | Tracks model name, version, parameters |

### Key Value Proposition

**For developers:** "When something goes wrong in AI-generated code, know exactly what was asked, what the model produced, and what the surrounding context was — without trying to reconstruct it from memory."

**For engineering leads:** "See your team's AI coding patterns: which models, which files, how much, and what risk level — across all developers in the workspace."

**For compliance/security teams:** "AI-generated code is now in your codebase. LineageLens gives you the audit trail to prove what was generated, when, by which model, and whether it contained sensitive patterns at insertion time."

